title Chess Server Design - Matthew Rahm
actor Client
participant Server
participant Handler
participant Service
participant DataAccess
database Database

// Proposed interactions for Phase 3; database operations describe the storage contract.
group #navy Register #white
Client -> Server: POST /user\n{username, password, email}
Server -> Handler: registerHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: deserialize JSON into RegisterRequest
break malformed JSON or incompatible field types
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Handler -> Service: register(RegisterRequest)
break request is null or username, password, or email is missing/null
Service --> Handler: throw BadRequestException
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getUser(username)
DataAccess -> Database: find user by username
Database --> DataAccess: UserData or null
DataAccess --> Service: user = UserData or null
break user is not null
Service --> Handler: throw AlreadyTakenException
Handler --> Server: 403 {"message":"Error: already taken"}
Server --> Client: 403 {"message":"Error: already taken"}
end
Service -> Service: passwordHash = hashPassword(password)
Service -> DataAccess: createUser(UserData(username, passwordHash, email))
DataAccess -> Database: store UserData
Database --> DataAccess: stored
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service -> Service: authToken = generateToken()\nusing UUID.randomUUID()
Service -> DataAccess: createAuth(AuthData(authToken, username))
DataAccess -> Database: store AuthData
Database --> DataAccess: stored
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service --> Handler: RegisterResult(username, authToken)
Handler -> Handler: serialize result to JSON
Handler --> Server: 200 {username, authToken}
Server --> Client: 200 {username, authToken}
end

// Alternative termination of Register if any data access operation fails.
group #gray Register storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During any database operation above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end

group #orange Login #white
Client -> Server: POST /session\n{username, password}
Server -> Handler: loginHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: deserialize JSON into LoginRequest
break malformed JSON or incompatible field types
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Handler -> Service: login(LoginRequest)
break request is null or username or password is missing/null
Service --> Handler: throw BadRequestException
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getUser(username)
DataAccess -> Database: find user by username
Database --> DataAccess: UserData or null
DataAccess --> Service: user = UserData or null
break user is null
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> Service: passwordMatches(password, user.password)
break password does not match the stored hash
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> Service: authToken = generateToken()\nusing UUID.randomUUID()
Service -> DataAccess: createAuth(AuthData(authToken, username))
DataAccess -> Database: store new AuthData; preserve other sessions
Database --> DataAccess: stored
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service --> Handler: LoginResult(username, authToken)
Handler -> Handler: serialize result to JSON
Handler --> Server: 200 {username, authToken}
Server --> Client: 200 {username, authToken}
end

// Alternative termination of Login if any data access operation fails.
group #gray Login storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During any database operation above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end

group #green Logout #white
Client -> Server: DELETE /session\nauthorization: authToken
Server -> Handler: logoutHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: read authorization header into LogoutRequest(authToken)
Handler -> Service: logout(LogoutRequest)
break authorization token is missing or empty
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getAuth(authToken)
DataAccess -> Database: find authorization by authToken
Database --> DataAccess: AuthData or null
DataAccess --> Service: auth = AuthData or null
break auth is null
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: deleteAuth(authToken)
DataAccess -> Database: remove only the matching authorization
Database --> DataAccess: deleted
DataAccess --> Service: return
note over Service,Database: Preserve users, games, and all other sessions.
Service --> Handler: return
Handler -> Handler: create empty JSON response {}
Handler --> Server: 200 {}
Server --> Client: 200 {}
end

// Alternative termination of Logout if either data access operation fails.
group #gray Logout storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During getAuth or deleteAuth above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end

group #gray Clear application #white
Client -> Server: DELETE /db
Server -> Handler: clearHandler(context)
Handler -> Service: clear()
Service -> DataAccess: clear()
DataAccess -> Database: remove all authorizations
Database --> DataAccess: removed
DataAccess -> Database: remove all games
Database --> DataAccess: removed
DataAccess -> Database: remove all users
Database --> DataAccess: removed
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service --> Handler: return
Handler -> Handler: create empty JSON response {}
Handler --> Server: 200 {}
Server --> Client: 200 {}
note over Client,Database: No authorization header or request body is required.\nAn already-empty store also succeeds.
end

// Alternative termination of Clear if any removal fails.
group #gray Clear storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During clear() above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end

group #red List Games #white
Client -> Server: GET /game\nauthorization: authToken
Server -> Handler: listGamesHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: read authorization header into ListGamesRequest(authToken)
Handler -> Service: listGames(ListGamesRequest)
break authorization token is missing or empty
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getAuth(authToken)
DataAccess -> Database: find authorization by authToken
Database --> DataAccess: AuthData or null
DataAccess --> Service: auth = AuthData or null
break auth is null
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: listGames()
DataAccess -> Database: retrieve all games
Database --> DataAccess: collection of GameData (possibly empty)
DataAccess --> Service: collection of GameData
Service -> Service: map each GameData to GameSummary\n(gameID, whiteUsername, blackUsername, gameName)
Service --> Handler: ListGamesResult(games)
Handler -> Handler: serialize result to JSON; include null player names
Handler --> Server: 200 {"games":[{gameID, whiteUsername, blackUsername, gameName}, ...]}
Server --> Client: 200 {"games":[{gameID, whiteUsername, blackUsername, gameName}, ...]}
note over Service,Database: Return all games, not just the caller's games.\nDo not modify games or sessions; omit the ChessGame state from the response.
note over Client,Handler: Empty store: 200 {"games":[]}\nUnoccupied seats: whiteUsername or blackUsername is null.
end

// Alternative termination of List Games if either data access operation fails.
group #gray List Games storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During getAuth or listGames above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end

group #purple Create Game #white
Client -> Server: POST /game\nauthorization: authToken\n{gameName}
Server -> Handler: createGameHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: read authorization header and deserialize JSON\ninto CreateGameRequest(authToken, gameName)
break malformed JSON or incompatible field types
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Handler -> Service: createGame(CreateGameRequest)
break authorization token is missing or empty
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getAuth(authToken)
DataAccess -> Database: find authorization by authToken
Database --> DataAccess: AuthData or null
DataAccess --> Service: auth = AuthData or null
break auth is null
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
break request is null or gameName is missing/null
Service --> Handler: throw BadRequestException
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Service -> Service: game = new ChessGame()\nstandard starting board; White moves first
Service -> DataAccess: createGame(gameName, game)
DataAccess -> Database: store new GameData with a unique gameID\n(gameID, null, null, gameName, game)
Database --> DataAccess: assigned gameID
DataAccess --> Service: gameID
Service --> Handler: CreateGameResult(gameID)
Handler -> Handler: serialize result to JSON
Handler --> Server: 200 {gameID}
Server --> Client: 200 {gameID}
note over Service,Database: Creating a game does not join the creator to either seat.\nBoth player names start as null; existing games remain unchanged.
end

// Alternative termination of Create Game if either data access operation fails.
group #gray Create Game storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During getAuth or createGame above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end

group #yellow Join Game #black
Client -> Server: PUT /game\nauthorization: authToken\n{playerColor, gameID}
Server -> Handler: joinGameHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: read authorization header and deserialize JSON\ninto JoinGameRequest(authToken, playerColor, gameID)
break malformed JSON or incompatible field types
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Handler -> Service: joinGame(JoinGameRequest)
break authorization token is missing or empty
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getAuth(authToken)
DataAccess -> Database: find authorization by authToken
Database --> DataAccess: AuthData or null
DataAccess --> Service: auth = AuthData or null
break auth is null
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
break request is null, gameID is missing/null, or playerColor is neither WHITE nor BLACK
Service --> Handler: throw BadRequestException
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getGame(gameID)
DataAccess -> Database: find game by gameID
Database --> DataAccess: GameData or null
DataAccess --> Service: game = GameData or null
break game is null
Service --> Handler: throw BadRequestException
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Service -> Service: inspect the player name for the requested color
break requested seat is already occupied
Service --> Handler: throw AlreadyTakenException
Handler --> Server: 403 {"message":"Error: already taken"}
Server --> Client: 403 {"message":"Error: already taken"}
end
alt playerColor is WHITE
Service -> Service: updatedGame = GameData(gameID, auth.username,\ngame.blackUsername, game.gameName, game.game)
else playerColor is BLACK
Service -> Service: updatedGame = GameData(gameID, game.whiteUsername,\nauth.username, game.gameName, game.game)
end
Service -> DataAccess: updateGame(updatedGame)
DataAccess -> Database: replace GameData for the existing gameID
Database --> DataAccess: updated
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service --> Handler: return
Handler -> Handler: create empty JSON response {}
Handler --> Server: 200 {}
Server --> Client: 200 {}
note over Service,Database: Use the username from AuthData, not from client input.\nPreserve the other seat, game name, board, and turn.\nRejected requests do not change the game.
end

// Alternative termination of Join Game if any data access operation fails.
group #gray Join Game storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During getAuth, getGame, or updateGame above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end
